scenario forecast over household_b
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "The story's forecast for 2026 – 2028 as we see it on 2026-01-02 (story.md, The forecast, points 1 – 9), which B-HR3 runs. Every figure is an assumption of the story, known 2026-01-02. Random facts are Tally's (L §5.16): their samples come from SHA-256 of their addresses, not from the story's Python stream, so the key's random figures are matched within their standard errors, not draw for draw."
  note "A month's project invoices are a Poisson count; each one's net and delay are random facts keyed by the month and a slot, and only the slots up to the month's count exist. Tally has no list of random length, so the slots are an index of six (proj_slots): a month with more than six projects (a chance near 1 in 1.6 million at mean 0.5) is cut to six."
  note "A scenario, not the base: the forecast is what the story assumes on 2026-01-02 about 2026 – 2028 (L §6.4), and its random facts must not make the base's own figures random (LOAD-RANDOM). Its rules join the base's defs through the version forecast_rules (replace rule with a new label, L §5.11 step 2)."
  note "fc_kessel_026, F5: Kessel pays the November invoice into the Lazur account by 2026-01-19; its due-day instance (2025-12-29) lies in the Lazur export's covered days with no row, so the base books no payment of it. The December invoice moves by a rule the version forecast_rules adds to the base's kessel_day."

index arnika_delays = 10..40

index living_slots = [first, second, third, fourth]

index proj_delays = 14..60

index proj_slots = 1..6

place fc_owed: claims DUK lives 2026-01-01..

input fc_arnika_back: (on date, inv key invoices, amount money DUK) question "When does Arnika-Delta pay the recalled invoice, and how much (F5)?"

input fc_arnika_net: money DUK question "What does Arnika-Delta pay net a month in 2026 – 2028 (F1)?"

input fc_bez_day: date question "When does Studio Bez pay the rest of its June invoice (F5)?"

input fc_bez_inv: key invoices question "Which invoice's rest does Studio Bez pay (F5)?"

input fc_fee: money DUK question "What is the building fee a month in the forecast (F3)?"

input fc_fee_dom: int question "On which day of the month is the building fee paid (F3)?"

input fc_flr_credit_day: date question "When are the sold florens credited to Cis (F5)?"

input fc_flr_rate: num DUK/FLR question "At what rate are the florens sold in January 2026 (F5)?"

input fc_flr_sell_day: date question "When are all the florens in the Lazur account sold (F5)?"

input fc_from: date question "From which day does the forecast run (story: 2026 to 2028)?"

input fc_it_hi: num question "What is the IT rate of PIT-10 (c) if the law changes (F7)?"

input fc_kessel_026_on: date question "When does Kessel pay the November invoice into the Lazur account (F5)?"

input fc_kessel_028_on: date question "When does Kessel pay the December invoice into the Lazur account (F5)?"

input fc_law_from: date question "From when would the IT rate change (F7)?"

input fc_law_odds: num question "With what odds is the IT rate 15 % from 2027, once for each path (F7)?"

input fc_living: money DUK question "How much living money leaves Cis each time (F3)?"

input fc_living_dom[w in living_slots]: int question "On which days of the month does living money leave Cis (F3)?"

input fc_plot: money DUK question "What does the building plot cost (F4)?"

input fc_plot_day: date question "When does the plot's money leave Cis (F4)?"

input fc_power: money DUK question "What is electricity a month (F3)?"

input fc_power_dom: int question "On which day of the month is electricity paid (F3)?"

input fc_proj_dom: int question "On which day of the month are project invoices issued (F2)?"

input fc_proj_mean: num question "What is the mean number of project invoices a month (F2)?"

input fc_proj_median: num question "What is a project's median net, in dukats (F2)?"

input fc_proj_sigma: num question "What is the sigma of a project net's logarithm (F2)?"

input hr3_line: money DUK question "Below what liquid money does B-HR3 count a path?"

input hr3_share: num question "Above what share of paths does B-HR3 stop the overpayments?"

input hr5_step: money DUK question "To which step is B-HR5's transfer rounded up?"

input hr5_target: money DUK question "To what does B-HR5 bring Cis at the end of the day?"

def fc_arnika_delay[m in months]: dist = discrete(1 for k in arnika_delays)

def fc_arnika_issue[m in months]: date = last_business(m, 1, holidays) at start_of(m)

def fc_law: dist = binomial(1, fc_law_odds)

def fc_live[m in months]: bool = start_of(m) >= fc_from

def fc_nproj[m in months]: dist = poisson(fc_proj_mean)

def fc_out_vat[m in months]: money DUK at start_of(m)
  rule none_r = 0 DUK
  rule fc beats none_r = round(fc_arnika_net * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up) + sum(round(fc_pnet_duk[m, s] * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up) for s in proj_slots where s <= fc_nproj[m]) when fc_live[m]

def fc_pdelay[m in months, s in proj_slots]: dist = discrete(1 for k in proj_delays)

def fc_pissue[m in months]: date = schedule(m, fc_proj_dom, following, holidays) at start_of(m)

def fc_pnet[m in months, s in proj_slots]: dist = lognormal(ln(fc_proj_median) to 1e-12, fc_proj_sigma) to 1

def fc_pnet_duk[m in months, s in proj_slots]: money DUK = round(fc_pnet[m, s] * 1 DUK, minor(DUK), half-up)

def fc_rev_part[m in months, s in pit10_supply]: money DUK
  rule none_r = 0 DUK
  rule fc beats none_r = fc_arnika_net + sum(fc_pnet_duk[m, k] for k in proj_slots where k <= fc_nproj[m]) when fc_live[m] and s == it

def liquid_low: money DUK = min(bal(cis, end_of(m) - 1) + bal(savings, end_of(m) - 1) for m in months where fc_live[m])

move fc_arnika_back_pay: transfers
  on fc_arnika_back.on
  leg cash from inv_owed[fc_arnika_back.inv] to cis amount fc_arnika_back.amount

move fc_arnika_inv[m in months]: transfers
  on fc_arnika_issue[m]
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m]
  leg cash from world to fc_owed amount fc_arnika_net + round(fc_arnika_net * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up)

move fc_arnika_pay[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(add_days(fc_arnika_issue[m], fc_arnika_delay[m]), holidays) then add_days(fc_arnika_issue[m], fc_arnika_delay[m]) else add_business(add_days(fc_arnika_issue[m], fc_arnika_delay[m]), 1, holidays)
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m]
  leg cash from fc_owed to cis amount fc_arnika_net + round(fc_arnika_net * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up)

move fc_bez_pay: transfers
  on fc_bez_day
  leg cash from inv_owed[fc_bez_inv] to cis amount sale[fc_bez_inv].net + sale[fc_bez_inv].vat - observed(client_pay[fc_bez_inv]).cash.amount

move fc_fee_pay[m in months]: transfers
  on schedule(m, fc_fee_dom, following, holidays)
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m]
  leg cash from cis to world amount fc_fee

move fc_flr_credit: transfers
  on fc_flr_credit_day
  reads fc_flr_sell
  leg cash from world to cis amount round(fc_flr_sell.cash.amount * fc_flr_rate, minor(DUK), half-up)

move fc_flr_sell: transfers
  on fc_flr_sell_day
  reads lazur
  leg cash from lazur to world amount bal(lazur)

move fc_kessel_026: transfers
  on fc_kessel_026_on
  leg cash from inv_owed_flr[fv_026_2025] to lazur amount sale_flr[fv_026_2025].net + sale_flr[fv_026_2025].vat

move fc_living_pay[m in months, w in living_slots]: transfers
  on schedule(m, fc_living_dom[w], following, holidays)
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m]
  leg cash from cis to shops amount fc_living

move fc_plot_pay: transfers
  on fc_plot_day
  leg cash from cis to world amount fc_plot

move fc_power_pay[m in months]: transfers
  on schedule(m, fc_power_dom, following, holidays)
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m]
  leg cash from cis to world amount fc_power

move fc_proj_inv[m in months, s in proj_slots]: transfers
  on fc_pissue[m]
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m] and s <= fc_nproj[m]
  leg cash from world to fc_owed amount fc_pnet_duk[m, s] + round(fc_pnet_duk[m, s] * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up)

move fc_proj_pay[m in months, s in proj_slots]: transfers
  on if is_business(add_days(fc_pissue[m], fc_pdelay[m, s]), holidays) then add_days(fc_pissue[m], fc_pdelay[m, s]) else add_business(add_days(fc_pissue[m], fc_pdelay[m, s]), 1, holidays)
  at start_of(m)
  when fc_live[m] and s <= fc_nproj[m]
  leg cash from fc_owed to cis amount fc_pnet_duk[m, s] + round(fc_pnet_duk[m, s] * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up)

move hr5_topup[d in days]: transfers
  on d
  at d
  when start_of(d) >= hr4_from and bal(cis) < 0 DUK
  reads cis
  after hr2_overpay
  after hr2_save
  leg cash from savings to cis amount round(hr5_target - bal(cis), hr5_step, up)

version story_forecast
  cite story
  governs always
  known 2026-01-02
  assumed "the story's forecast for 2026 – 2028, as seen on 2026-01-02 (story.md, The forecast)"
  fc_arnika_back = (on: 2026-01-08, inv: fv_023_2025, amount: 19520.00 DUK) "F5: Arnika-Delta's 19 520.00 DUK on 2026-01-08 (B-D19)"
  fc_arnika_net = 16000.00 DUK "F1: 16 000.00 DUK net a month, VAT added, invoiced on the last business day"
  fc_bez_day = 2026-01-15 "F5: Studio Bez's rest on 2026-01-15"
  fc_bez_inv = fv_011_2025 "F5: the rest of its June invoice (B-D20)"
  fc_fee = 690.00 DUK "F3: the building fee 690.00 DUK on the 10th"
  fc_fee_dom = 10 "F3: on the 10th"
  fc_flr_credit_day = 2026-01-21 "F5: credited to Cis on 2026-01-21"
  fc_flr_rate = 4.15 DUK/FLR "F5: every floren sold at 4.15 DUK"
  fc_flr_sell_day = 2026-01-20 "F5: on 2026-01-20 every floren there is sold"
  fc_from = 2026-01-01 "story: for 2026 to 2028"
  fc_it_hi = 0.15 "F7: the IT rate of PIT-10 (c) is 15 % from January 2027"
  fc_kessel_026_on = 2026-01-19 "F5: Kessel pays the November and December invoices into the Lazur account by 2026-01-19"
  fc_kessel_028_on = 2026-01-19 "F5: Kessel pays the November and December invoices into the Lazur account by 2026-01-19"
  fc_law_from = 2027-01-01 "F7: from January 2027 on"
  fc_law_odds = 0.30 "F7: once for each path, with odds of 0.30"
  fc_living = 2375.00 DUK "F3: 2 375.00 DUK on the 1st, 8th, 15th and 22nd"
  fc_living_dom[first] = 1 "F3: the 1st"
  fc_living_dom[second] = 8 "F3: the 8th"
  fc_living_dom[third] = 15 "F3: the 15th"
  fc_living_dom[fourth] = 22 "F3: the 22nd"
  fc_plot = 180000.00 DUK "F4: the building plot, 180 000.00 DUK"
  fc_plot_day = 2026-09-15 "F4: leaves Cis on 2026-09-15"
  fc_power = 175.00 DUK "F3: electricity 175.00 DUK on the 12th"
  fc_power_dom = 12 "F3: on the 12th"
  fc_proj_dom = 15 "F2: issued on the 15th (or the next business day)"
  fc_proj_mean = 0.5 "F2: a Poisson number of project invoices, mean 0.5"
  fc_proj_median = 8000 "F2: each one's net lognormal, median 8 000.00 DUK"
  fc_proj_sigma = 0.5 "F2: sigma 0.5 of its logarithm"
  hr3_line = 60000.00 DUK "B-HR3: below 60 000.00 DUK"
  hr3_share = 0.20 "B-HR3: more than one path in five"

version hr5_rule
  cite house_rules
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  note "B-HR5 is a house rule from 2025-01-01, not a figure of the story's forecast: its rows are known from then, before the scenario's from (2026-01-01)"
  hr5_step = 100.00 DUK "B-HR5: rounded up to the next 100.00 DUK"
  hr5_target = 1000.00 DUK "B-HR5: to bring Cis to 1 000.00 DUK at the end of the day"

version forecast_figures
  cite story
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  assumed "F6: the forecast's own figures, where no notice is published yet"
  avg_wage_proj = 9900.00 DUK governs 2027-01-01..2027-12-31 "F6: AVG-WAGE-PROJ 9 900.00 DUK for 2027"
  avg_wage_proj = 10500.00 DUK governs 2028-01-01..2028-12-31 "F6: AVG-WAGE-PROJ 10 500.00 DUK for 2028"
  avg_wage_q4 = 9200.00 DUK governs 2026-02-01..2027-01-31 "F6: AVG-WAGE-Q4 9 200.00 DUK from February 2026"
  avg_wage_q4 = 9800.00 DUK governs 2027-02-01..2028-01-31 "F6: AVG-WAGE-Q4 9 800.00 DUK from February 2027"
  avg_wage_q4 = 10400.00 DUK governs 2028-02-01..2029-01-31 "F6: AVG-WAGE-Q4 10 400.00 DUK from February 2028"

version forecast_rules
  cite story
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  assumed "the story's forecast joins the base's defs: its revenue and VAT (F1, F2), F7's law draw"
  replace rule flat_rate.drawn beats elected = (if fc_law == 1 then fc_it_hi else pit10_flat_rate[s]) when s == it and start_of(m) >= fc_law_from and biz_form == flat
  replace rule out_vat.fc beats booked = sum(round(sale[i].net * vat_rate, minor(DUK), half-up) for i in invoices where month_of(sale[i].issued) == m and vat_on[sale[i].issued]) + sum(vat_flr[j] for j in flr_invoices where month_of(sale_flr[j].issued) == m and vat_on[sale_flr[j].issued]) + fc_out_vat[m] when fc_live[m]
  replace rule rev_part.fc beats booked = sum(sale[i].net for i in invoices where month_of(sale[i].issued) == m and sale[i].sup == s) + sum(rev_flr[j] for j in flr_invoices where month_of(sale_flr[j].issued) == m and sale_flr[j].sup == s) + fc_rev_part[m, s] when fc_live[m]
  replace rule kessel_day.f5 beats due = fc_kessel_028_on when j == fv_028_2025
